# Documentation
# Generated docs (codebase_reference.md) stay untracked; the two hand-written
# ones are part of the project.
*.md
!README.md

# Generated report, same convention as the *.md audits above. Scoped to the
# root so static/index.html — which the game actually serves — stays tracked.
/RUNBOOK.html

# Conversation transcripts dropped in the repo root by /export. Date-prefixed
# and root-scoped so python/requirements.txt is not caught by it.
/20??-??-??-*.txt
!CLAUDE.md
# Hand-written reference, same standing as README and CLAUDE. The *.md rule
# above exists for generated audits, not for docs that are part of the project.
!CODEBASE.md

# Per-host compose overrides. Editing the tracked compose on a server means
# every `git pull` conflicts; put deployment-specific deviations here instead
# and pass both files with -f. See the header of docker-compose.game.yml.
/compose.local.yml
